<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Plateforme Énergie – Simulations interactives</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<style>
body{
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  margin:0;
  background:#f4f6f8;
}
header{
  background:#0d6efd;
  color:white;
  padding:20px;
  text-align:center;
}
section{
  background:white;
  margin:20px auto;
  padding:20px;
  max-width:1000px;
  border-radius:8px;
  box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}
h2{color:#0d6efd;}
iframe{
  width:100%;
  height:500px;
  border:none;
}
footer{
  text-align:center;
  color:#666;
  padding:15px;
}
canvas{
  display:block;
  margin:auto;
  border:1px solid #ccc;
}
</style>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/p5@1.6.0/lib/p5.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-latest.min.js"></script>
</head>

<body>

<header>
<h1>Plateforme interactive – Énergie</h1>
<p>Simulations pédagogiques – Physique</p>
</header>

<section>
<h2>1️⃣ Transformations de l’énergie (PhET)</h2>
<p>Explore les conversions entre énergie thermique, mécanique et interne.</p>

<iframe src="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/energy-forms-and-changes/latest/energy-forms-and-changes_fr.html"></iframe>
</section>

<section>
<h2>2️⃣ Énergie interne et agitation microscopique</h2>
<p>Plus la température augmente, plus l’agitation des particules est importante.</p>

<div id="p5-container"></div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>3️⃣ Diagramme Pression – Volume (PV)</h2>
<p>Le travail d’un gaz correspond à l’aire sous la courbe PV.</p>

<div id="pv-graph" style="width:100%;height:450px;"></div>
</section>

<footer>
Plateforme Énergie – Maroc 🇲🇦
</footer>

<script>
let particles=[];
function setup(){
  let canvas=createCanvas(600,350);
  canvas.parent("p5-container");
  for(let i=0;i<120;i++){
    particles.push({
      x:random(width),
      y:random(height),
      vx:random(-2,2),
      vy:random(-2,2)
    });
  }
}
function draw(){
  background(245);
  particles.forEach(p=>{
    p.x+=p.vx;
    p.y+=p.vy;
    if(p.x<0||p.x>width)p.vx*=-1;
    if(p.y<0||p.y>height)p.vy*=-1;
    fill(13,110,253);
    noStroke();
    circle(p.x,p.y,6);
  });
}
</script>

<script>
var trace={
  x:[1,2,3,4,5],
  y:[8,6,5,4,3],
  mode:'lines+markers'
};
var layout={
  title:'Diagramme PV',
  xaxis:{title:'Volume'},
  yaxis:{title:'Pression'}
};
Plotly.newPlot('pv-graph',[trace],layout);
</script>

</body>
</html>
